e + N2(X) -> e + N2(a_1Pi_g). Su et al. J. Phys. B 54, 115203 (2021) (CC BY 4.0) below 20 eV; Johnson et al. J. Geophys. Res. 110, A11311 (2005) Table 2 from 20 eV; power-law continuation p = 1.07 above Johnson's last point (to 10 keV). Overlap Su/Johnson: 12.5 eV 1.77 (+-0.17), 15 eV 0.99 (+-0.18), 17.5 eV 0.96 (+-0.18), 20 eV 0.84 (+-0.18); step at 20 eV Su/Johnson = 0.84. Continuation share of the rate: T_e 20 eV 0.0 % (zero/hold tail -0.0/+0.0 %), T_e 30 eV 0.2 % (zero/hold tail -0.2/+0.0 %). Header 9.31 eV = experimental vertical excitation energy (Oddershede, Su 2021 Table 1); no threshold shift. Maxwellian-integrated by abep_sim/rate_tables.py (scripts/build_n2_electronic_excitation_tables.py). Reaction set abep-n2n-0.9.
